# Global gitignore (core.excludesfile).
#
# Changed from the 2022 version: .envrc and .tool-versions are no longer
# ignored. Both are per-project files that belong in a project's repo — a
# committed .envrc is how a team shares non-secret environment setup, and
# .tool-versions is how mise pins runtimes for everyone. Ignoring them globally
# meant they could never be committed anywhere. .envrc.local takes their place
# here as the machine-local, secret-bearing counterpart.

# --- macOS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- Windows (for repos shared with Windows machines) ------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- editors and tools -------------------------------------------------------
# Vim swap and session files
[._]*.s[a-w][a-z]
[._]s[a-w][a-z]
*.un~
Session.vim
.netrwhist
*~

# --- ctags / cscope ----------------------------------------------------------
TAGS
!TAGS/
tags
!tags/
.tags
.tags1
gtags.files
GTAGS
GRTAGS
GPATH
cscope.files
cscope.out
cscope.in.out
cscope.po.out

# --- build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
.sass-cache

# --- local environment overrides ---------------------------------------------
# Machine-local secrets for direnv. The project's .envrc should source this if
# present and commit only the non-secret parts. See docs/mise-direnv.md.
.envrc.local

# mise's generated lockfile. Ignored while none of the repos in use track it, so
# it would otherwise show up as untracked noise in every project.
#
# Note this is the opposite call from mise.toml and .tool-versions above, and the
# distinction is intent vs. artifact: those files declare which versions a
# project wants and belong to the project, whereas mise.lock is generated output
# pinning exact resolved versions.
#
# Two things worth knowing:
#   - A repo that DOES track mise.lock is unaffected. gitignore has no say over
#     files git already tracks.
#   - To commit one deliberately in your own project: git add -f mise.lock
mise.lock
